{{!
    @template local_unlistedcourses/applydefault_setting

    The "Apply the default to existing courses" item of the settings page.

    Rendered from local_unlistedcourses\local\admin\setting_applydefault. The row keeps the
    markup of core_admin/setting_description, so the item lines up with the other settings.
    Every string arrives already translated and in its plain spelling, escaped here by the
    double stash it lands in.

    Context variables required for this template - named in prose, because a Mustache
    comment ends at its first closing pair and a tag written here would truncate it:

    * title - string, the setting's title, shown in the label column.
    * reach - string, the first paragraph: what the default does not reach.
    * next - string, the second paragraph: what the confirmation page shows.
    * url - string, the confirmation page's URL.
    * action - string, the button's label.
    * savefirst - string, the note beside the button.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "title": "Apply the default to existing courses",
        "reach": "The default above only reaches courses created from now on. Courses that already exist and never had a discoverability set stay Listed.",
        "next": "The next page shows how many courses will change and asks for confirmation before changing any of them.",
        "url": "https://example.com/local/unlistedcourses/applydefault.php",
        "action": "Apply to existing courses",
        "savefirst": "Save changes first: the action uses the saved default."
    }
}}
<div class="form-item row">
    <div class="form-label col-sm-3 text-sm-end">
        <label>{{title}}</label>
    </div>
    <div class="form-setting col-sm-9">
        <div class="form-text mt-0 mb-3">
            <p class="mb-2">{{reach}}</p>
            <p class="mb-0">{{next}}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="d-flex flex-wrap align-items-center gap-2">
            <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="{{url}}">{{action}}</a>
            <span class="text-muted small">{{savefirst}}</span>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
